  {
   "type": "title",
   "title": "The week on the network",
   "secs": 15,
   "say": "Graham Watts, with the week on the network. A wet one. Our base station began hearing four times the stations it did, and at the end of the week the Hillcrest repeater faded. Might as well start at the beginning."
  },
  {
   "type": "trend",
   "title": "The fortnight, in two halves",
   "sub": "most of the change is how we listen",
   "secs": 18,
   "say": "First, the shape of the fortnight. Until Sunday the eighteenth, the base station heard about three hundred stations a day and missed three checks in five. On Monday it got a second stick and the ALERT2 channel. Stations heard went to over a thousand, checks received to about eighty per cent. That's us hearing more, not the network getting better.",
