  {
   "type": "list",
   "title": "Who sent the bit flips",
   "sub": "by the carrier on the corrupted copies",
   "presenter": "tech-wizard",
   "sev": "warn",
   "secs": 21,
   "say": "Alex Chen, with the bit flips. Hillcrest and Toowoomba sent back half of what they relayed with bits wrong, as strong as the clean copies — so the error starts at them. Mount Glorious and Schultz Lookout are busier and cleaner, four or five per cent. And the flips keep no hours, which points at equipment more than a neighbour's interference.",
   "stations": [
